---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<Page
  title="Contact"
  description="Report a bug, correct an out-of-date platform specification, or suggest a tool. Email only, no form and no tracking."
  h1="Contact"
  path="/contact/"
  blurb="One email address, read by a person. There is no form here because a form would need a server, and this site deliberately does not have one."
>
  <p style="font-size: var(--step-2); font-weight: 600; margin-top: var(--space-6)">
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
  </p>

  <h2>Especially useful to hear about</h2>

  <h3>A platform specification that has changed</h3>
  <p>
    Image size requirements move without announcement, and an out-of-date number here is worse
    than no number at all. If a preset or a guide is wrong, tell us which one and what it should
    be. A link to the platform's own documentation makes the fix immediate.
  </p>

  <h3>A file that will not process</h3>
  <p>
    If a tool fails on one of your files, the useful details are: which tool, what the file came
    from (which camera, phone or program made it), which browser you are using, and any message
    that appeared. Please do not attach the file to a first email — describe it instead, and we
    will ask if we need more.
  </p>

  <h3>A result that looks wrong</h3>
  <p>
    Rotated output, shifted colours, a DPI value that did not take effect, transparency that
    turned black — these are bugs, and specific reports are what fix them.
  </p>

  <h3>A tool that should exist</h3>
  <p>
    Suggestions are welcome, particularly if you can describe the actual task you were trying to
    complete rather than the feature you imagined. The task is usually more informative.
  </p>

  <h2>What we cannot help with</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Recovering a file. Nothing you process is ever sent to us, so there is no copy on our side
      to retrieve.
    </li>
    <li>
      Account problems on Etsy, Amazon, eBay, YouTube or anywhere else. We have no relationship
      with those companies.
    </li>
    <li>Editing your images for you.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Response times</h2>
  <p>
    This is a small project rather than a company with a support desk. Email gets read, and
    genuine bug reports get priority, but a reply may take a few days.
  </p>

  {/* Deliberately no ad slots: Google prohibits ads on thin utility pages. */}
</Page>
